==============================================================================
0) BIG PICTURE — WHAT IS PARTITIONING?
==============================================================================

INTUITION:
Socho tumhare paas ek single database server hai jisme:
- 1 billion users
- 10 billion messages
- 100 TB data

Ek machine:
→ slow ho jayegi
→ memory overflow
→ disk I/O bottleneck
→ queries slow

Solution:
Divide data across multiple machines.

THIS = PARTITIONING (a.k.a SHARDING)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
REAL LIFE ANALOGY
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Library example:

Ek library me 10 million books.
Agar sab books ek hi shelf pe:
→ impossible to search

So library splits:
- A–F → Shelf 1
- G–M → Shelf 2
- N–Z → Shelf 3

Now:
→ faster lookup
→ parallel access
→ scalable

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CORE IDEA
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Partitioning = splitting large dataset into smaller independent chunks
Each chunk = partition / shard

Each partition:
- stored on separate node
- queried independently

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY PARTITIONING?
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1) Horizontal scaling
2) Parallel query execution
3) Reduced latency
4) Better cache locality
5) Fault isolation

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARCHITECTURE THINKING
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Client → Router / API → Decide partition → Forward request

Partition key = decides where data goes

CRITICAL DESIGN QUESTION:
"What is your partition key?"

Bad key = hotspot
Good key = balanced system

